{
  "_comment": [
    "REFERENCE ONLY — this project does NOT use google-services.json at",
    "runtime. Firebase is initialised manually via Firebase.initializeApp",
    "(options:), with the options sealed (encrypted) in the Rust vault so no",
    "plaintext credentials ship in the APK. This stub only documents which",
    "fields map to the vault selectors.",
    "  project_number    -> V_PROJECT_NUMBER (sel 4, == messagingSenderId)",
    "  api_key.current_key -> V_FB_API_KEY        (sel 60)",
    "  mobilesdk_app_id   -> V_FB_APP_ID          (sel 61)",
    "  project_id         -> V_FB_PROJECT_ID      (sel 62)",
    "  storage_bucket     -> V_FB_STORAGE_BUCKET  (sel 63)",
    "To rotate the config: reseal those arrays with the dev helper in",
    "native/stonewatch_core/src/mask.rs and rebuild. Do NOT drop a real",
    "google-services.json next to this file — the Gradle plugin would then",
    "bake the plaintext config into APK resources, defeating the vault."
  ],
  "project_info": {
    "project_number": "000000000000",
    "project_id": "REPLACE_ME",
    "storage_bucket": "REPLACE_ME.firebasestorage.app"
  },
  "client": [
    {
      "client_info": {
        "mobilesdk_app_id": "1:000000000000:android:0000000000000000000000",
        "android_client_info": {
          "package_name": "com.stonewatch.watchgame"
        }
      },
      "oauth_client": [],
      "api_key": [
        { "current_key": "REPLACE_ME" }
      ],
      "services": {
        "appinvite_service": { "other_platform_oauth_client": [] }
      }
    }
  ],
  "configuration_version": "1"
}
